# What the image build must NOT be handed.
#
# There was no such file, which was survivable while the CI checkout was shallow
# and nobody built the image on their own machine. Both of those stopped being
# true: the container workflow now clones the full history so that `git describe`
# has tags to describe against, and that history is 28 MB of build context sent
# to the daemon twice per run for a file the build never opens.
#
# The size is the boring half. The correctness half is `web/node_modules`:
# the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and only THEN does `COPY web/ ./web/`, so a
# node_modules directory sitting in the context would be copied straight over
# the one the build just installed. On a developer's machine that means Windows
# or macOS binaries landing in a Linux image, which fails in a way that has
# nothing to do with the change being tested.

# Version control. The build never reads it; the workflow computes the version
# stamp before the build and passes it in as a build argument.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Installed and generated by the build itself, in the build.
web/node_modules
web/dist
node_modules

# Desktop shell output and its own embedded copy of the interface.
desktop/build/bin
desktop/frontend/dist

# Go build and test output.
*.exe
*.test

# Documentation, CI definitions and delivery templates: none of it is copied by
# any stage, and all of it changes often enough to be worth keeping out of the
# context on its own.
.github
docs
templates
scripts
*.md
LICENSE

# Local scratch that must never end up in an image.
smoke-config
.playwright-mcp
